        {
          "title": "Job Description",
          "icon": "fa-solid fa-file-alt",
          "iconColor": "#28B463",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "<div class=\"pdf-container\">\n  <iframe src=\"documents/mechanical/Tesla/Job_Description.pdf\" width=\"100%\" height=\"600px\"></iframe>\n</div>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Summary",
          "icon": "fa-solid fa-align-left",
          "iconColor": "#E67E22",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "<div class=\"summary-container\"><div class=\"summary-text\"><p>I had the incredible opportunity to work as a <strong>Mechanical Design Engineer</strong> in the Bay Area, USA, as part of the <strong>Thermal Team</strong>, which is known for owning one of the best-engineered vehicle thermal systems in the world.<br><br>As a key member of the thermal team, I was responsible for seven thermal coolant hose bundles spanning two future vehicles (CyberCab and Cybertruck RWD). I led various investigations, from material selection to automation design. My role involved the full iterative process of design, prototyping, and testing, gaining hands-on experience in <strong>designing for manufacturing (DFM)</strong> and automation.<br><br>One of my significant contributions was leading the <strong>RFQ (Request for Quote)</strong> process for one of the future vehicles. This included coordinating ongoing meetings with multiple suppliers to ensure the design was ready for mass production. My efforts culminated in giving the go-ahead for over $160k in tools, which helped the company save over $100k annually, all while the components were projected to cost over $1 million a year.<br><br>What stood out most during my time at Tesla was the company's unique flat organizational structure. Despite the global challenges faced by large tech companies, Tesla operates with a lean, trusting approach that places significant ownership in its employees. This allowed me to accomplish and grow in ways I never expected, and I'm incredibly grateful for the opportunity.<br><br>Applying the knowledge I gained at Monash University, including Solid Mechanics, Dynamics, Thermal, Materials, and Tolerancing, was instrumental in my day-to-day work. I also expanded my knowledge with new topics like NVH (Noise, Vibration, and Harshness) and durability, which were critical in ensuring the success of my projects.</p></div><div class=\"summary-media\"><img src=\"images/mechanical/Tesla/Tesla_Factory.jpg\" alt=\"Tesla Factory\"><img src=\"images/mechanical/Tesla/Tesla_Cars.jpg\" alt=\"Tesla Cars\"><img src=\"images/mechanical/Tesla/Tesla_Fremont.jpg\" alt=\"Tesla Fremont Factory\"><div class=\"video-container\"><iframe width=\"100%\" height=\"200\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/Qfj4urMF8CU\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen></iframe></div></div></div>"
            }
          ]
        },
